{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-75407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The unit tangent vector to a curve at an arbitrary point is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the principal normal vector at the point where $t=1$, if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q(1)=-i+j+\\frac{1}{2}k,\\,{q}^{′}(1)=j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-75407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot q(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}+2})\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(q(t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4t}{({t}^{2}+2)^{2}}\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot {q}^{′}(t) \\\\  \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =-\\frac{4(1)}{({1}^{2}+2)^{2}}\\cdot q(1)+\\frac{2}{{1}^{2}+2}\\cdot {q}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{9}(-i+j+\\frac{1}{2}k)+\\frac{2}{3}(j+k) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}\\,i+\\frac{2}{9}\\,j+\\frac{4}{9}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{4}{9})}^{2}+{(\\frac{2}{9})}^{2}+{(\\frac{4}{9})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{81}+\\frac{4}{81}+\\frac{16}{81}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{36}{81}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve at the point where $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(1) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(1)}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{4}{9}\\,i+\\frac{2}{9}\\,j+\\frac{4}{9}\\,k}{(\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j+\\frac{2}{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that when we find the scalar product of $T$ and $N$ at the point where $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1)\\cdot N(1) & =\\frac{2}{3}q(1)\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j+\\frac{2}{3}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(-i+j+\\frac{1}{2}k)\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j+\\frac{2}{3}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(-\\frac{2}{3}\\,i\\cdot \\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j\\cdot j+\\frac{1}{3}\\,k\\cdot k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-75407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fa988b8c46849704f7aa229fa69823b8c9d7d7cdf509fab6e5df322520ef0c22"} {"question" "q-75407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-75407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j+\\frac{2}{3}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\,j-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\,k"] ["math" "i"] ["math" "k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-75407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j+\\frac{2}{3}\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-127583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The unit tangent vector to a curve at an arbitrary point is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{2}{4+t}\\cdot q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the principal normal vector at the point where $t=0,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q(0)=⟨1,\\sqrt{3}⟩,\\,{q}^{′}(0)=⟨1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-127583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{4+t}\\cdot q(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{4+t})\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{2}{4+t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(q(t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{(4+t)}^{2}}\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{2}{4+t}\\cdot {q}^{′}(t) \\\\  \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{2}{{(4+0)}^{2}}\\cdot q(0)+\\frac{2}{4+0}\\cdot {q}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}⟨1,\\sqrt{3}⟩+\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(-⟨1,\\sqrt{3}⟩+4⟨1,0⟩) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}⟨3,-\\sqrt{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\frac{1}{8}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(0)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve at the point where $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{8}⟨3,-\\sqrt{3}⟩}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that when we find the scalar product of $T$ and $N$ at the point where $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0)\\cdot N(0) & =\\frac{1}{2}q(0)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,\\sqrt{3}⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-127583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fa988b8c46849704f7aa229fa69823b8c9d7d7cdf509fab6e5df322520ef0c22"} {"question" "q-127583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-127583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}⟨-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\sqrt{2},1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-127583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-223096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nT(t)=\\frac{1}{5}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+3\\,k).\n$$\n\nThe unit tangent vector to a curve at an arbitrary point is given above. Find the principal normal vector to that curve at an arbitrary point on the curve.\n\n$N(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-223096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{5}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+3\\,k)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(-4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3)\\,k) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{4}{5}‖\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\frac{4}{5}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)}{\\frac{4}{5}} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-223096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fa988b8c46849704f7aa229fa69823b8c9d7d7cdf509fab6e5df322520ef0c22"} {"question" "q-223096" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-223096" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\cos(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-223114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3t,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$, find the principal normal vector $N(t)$ at an arbitrary point on the curve.\n\n$N(t)=⟨$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,0\\,,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-223114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the unit tangent vector $T(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(3)^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3}{5}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0,\\,\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{(\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{25}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{4}{5}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩}{(\\frac{4}{5})} \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-223114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fa988b8c46849704f7aa229fa69823b8c9d7d7cdf509fab6e5df322520ef0c22"} {"question" "q-223114" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-223114" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\cos(t)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-358783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,4t⟩$, find the principal normal vector $N(t)$ at an arbitrary point on the curve.\n\n$N(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$\n{{field-1}}$,0\\,⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-358783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the unit tangent vector $T(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{4}{5}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{3}{5}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0⟩}{(\\frac{3}{5})}=⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073930/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e1ff99b2e0e2f7830d5becfb2b54056f78890adf0b6d104bf3e3ade0a474586"} {"question" "q-358783" "fie